'20261122_2015_M7_m8_candidate_baseline_verification.sql','2026-11-22T20:15:00+08:00','Win-M7','M7','role/M7-audit','DeepSeek Harness',
'AI was used to drive Access DAO over a temp copy of the database, export the three reports to PDF, and draft this receipt from the captured numbers. The auditor read the exported PDFs and the Access window before accepting the counts.',
'Baseline verification receipt for the M8 Group3 candidate database at commit 34b5587, requested by the group lead before human review of the relationship report labels and the REA diagram.',
'Counts were reproduced with DAO on a temp copy instead of the repository file because opening the tracked .accdb directly in Access rewrites it (observed 1060864 -> 1200128 bytes, SHA256 02A83541FEDDE73D...F8676 -> B910E13562E2...A1AC); the repository copy was restored from Git and re-hashed to 02A83541FEDDE73D6762BAAF194B3FFAFFE3B35627DFA62360A8078D48F8676 before any check. The original Database Documenter export is still blocked (Property not found / Disabled Mode) and the archived Table_Definitions_Documenter.pdf points at an older v2_R5 file, so the documenter deliverable is not counted as verified.',
'Group3_animalhospital.accdb SHA256 02A835410FEDDE73D6762BAAF194B3FFAFFE3B35627DFA62360A8078D48F8676, 1060864 bytes, at commit 34b55876813de7dad6f653ced3c42b2884c8144b; temp copy %TEMP%\m8_verify\Group3_verify.accdb; exported PDFs %TEMP%\m8_verify\out\rpt_00_Relationships_Report.pdf (26257 B, 1 page 842x595), rpt_01_REA_Diagram.pdf (160403 B, 1 page), rpt_02_System_Design_Notes.pdf (75445 B, 1 page 595x842); DAO output captured in this session.',
'Assumed reading a byte-identical temp copy is equivalent to reading the tracked file, and that DAO counts (record counts, PK via table indexes, relation attributes) are the authoritative engine view. Assumed the Documenter PDF is pending rather than failed because M8 has not re-exported it yet.',
'handoff_logs/entries/20261122_2015_M7_m8_candidate_baseline_verification.sql',
'PARTIAL',
'Tables 10, rows 21 (tblMedication 3, other nine 2 each), fields 46, field Description non-empty 46/46 (read via Field Properties("Description"); PowerShell direct .Description returns empty and must not be trusted). Primary keys via table indexes: 7 single-column (AccountID, ReceiptID, MedicationID, PetID, ParentID, VetID, AppointmentID) plus 3 composite (tblPrescriptionLine AppointmentID+MedicationID; tblReceiptAllocation ReceiptID+AppointmentID; tblMedicationInteraction MedicationAID+MedicationBID). Relations 12 (rel_1..rel_12), Attributes all 0. Queries 11 with row counts 2,2,2,1,1,2,2,2,3,1,0 matching the M8 report; qry_04 returns A1 205/205/0 and A2 90/0/90. Reports 3 (rpt_00, rpt_01, rpt_02); rpt_01 Image0 is embedded (PictureType 0, SizeMode 3, 147098 bytes) so the REA diagram renders offline; the rpt_00 PDF text layer contains all 10 table names and the long field names InteractionDescription, Diagnosis, AppointmentFee, so the label fix is present at the data level. What remains untested: visual clipping of the relationship labels, the new Database Documenter PDF, and candidate databases U01-U07.',
'Documenter PDF pending re-export by M8; native Database Documenter export still blocked by Property not found / Disabled Mode; T21 and T22 remain KNOWN_LIMITATION.',
'Human review of the exported report PDFs and the Access copy is the next step before the receipt is treated as final. Do not open the tracked .accdb directly in Access; use a copy outside the repository and restore with git restore workspaces/R8_Reports_UAT/Group3_animalhospital.accdb if the hash has changed.'
